# L §5.3 An entry is dated twice: "A thing entered by version V is seen only by asks with K ≥ V's known (earlier
# asks don't list it, and a read of it is refused, RUN-KEY)".  ben enters by a version known 2016-02-01:
# as known 2016-01-15 the listing holds ana only and a read of ben is RUN-KEY.
=== m.tally
model t
  tally 2
  on 2016-03-01
  start 2015-11-01
  end 2016-10-31

source s "s"

kind persons

input age_of[p in persons]: int

version a1
  cite s
  governs always
  known 2016-01-01
  persons + [ana] lives 1990-01-01..
  age_of[ana] = 26

version b1
  cite s
  governs always
  known 2016-02-01
  persons + [ben] lives 1991-01-01..
  age_of[ben] = 25

ask q1: count(p in persons on 2016-03-01) as known 2016-01-15
ask q2: age_of[ben] as known 2016-01-15
ask q3: count(p in persons on 2016-03-01)
=== expect
q1: 1
  cut 2016-01-15
q2: refused: RUN-KEY ...
  cut 2016-01-15
q3: 2
  cut 2016-03-01
